  "question": {
    "text": "<p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>A radioactive sample contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>2.2</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mg</mi></math> of pure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>6</mn><mn>11</mn></mmultiscripts></math> which has a half-life period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1224</mn></math> seconds. Calculate the number of atoms present initially, and the activity when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>μg</mi></math> of the sample will be left.</span></p>\r",
